# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Build output. `make package` writes here and `make clean` removes it; the
# root of the tree holds sources and configuration, never a built artifact.
build/
dist/
*.whl
*.tar.gz
!tests/fixtures/**/*.tar.gz

# Local environments and editor state.
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Two lines, in this order, and both are needed. `.vscode/` above excludes the
# DIRECTORY, and git will not re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, so un-ignoring the contents alone does nothing: the walk never
# descends. The first line re-includes the directory, the second its contents.
#
# They exist because `.vscode/tasks.json` is HALF OF THE ATTACK phase S1 is
# written about. Both 2026 npm worms plant a `runOn: folderOpen` task there, the
# fixtures carry it so the report can name it as not read in this release, and
# `git add -A` silently skipped both files - green on the machine that wrote
# them, red on a clean clone. `tests/test_fixtures_are_published.py` is the
# invariant now; this is the exception it needs to be satisfiable.
!tests/fixtures/**/.vscode/
!tests/fixtures/**/.vscode/**

# Coverage.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# Generated corpora. Every one of these is written from code at build time, so
# no malware is ever committed here: `evals/corpus/build.py` writes working
# gadget pickles, and the argument for generating them is in SECURITY.md.
evals/artifacts/
evals/_tamper/
evals/real/
evals/marking/artifacts/
evals/marking/_control.png
models/

# Fuzzing run output. The reduced regression inputs in fuzz/corpus/ ARE tracked.
fuzz/runs/

# Everything `make eval`, `make benchmark` or a stray run leaves behind.
*.zip
!tests/fixtures/*.zip
# fickling writes its scan output here on every `make benchmark`, appending to
# whatever was there before. Tracking it meant a benchmark run produced a
# 300 KB diff of somebody else's tool output on top of the previous run's, and
# reviewing it told a reader nothing.
safety_results.json

# `evals/benchmark.json` is deliberately NOT ignored, and neither are
# `evals/results.json`, `evals/marking/results.json` or
# `evals/agents/results.json`: docs/FIGURES.md and both READMEs quote figures
# from them, and an untracked source means the figure is only comparable on a
# machine with picklescan, modelscan and fickling installed. Regenerate with
# `make benchmark`; the versions it ran against are recorded inside the file.

# Screenshots. `make screenshots` writes every capture here first; only the six
# that a README or a doc actually displays are copied into docs/img/, and an
# image nothing displays is not documentation. See scripts/screenshots.py.
.screenshots/

# The closing plan this pass was worked from. It is a planning document about
# the repository, not part of it, and it should not travel inside a source
# archive of the product. Left on disk deliberately; only kept out of what
# ships.
Actaira_2.2.0_Plan_Final_Pulido_Repo_Local.md
Claude Code — Actaira Graph + Impact.md
Actaira — Evidence + Change Assurance Increment.md
ACTAIRA-PLAN-MAESTRO.md
.corpus/

# Launch material: the Marketplace listing text and the checklist for running
# the Action against real repositories. Both are about publishing the product
# rather than part of it, so they live on disk and never in the tree - the same
# argument the planning documents above are kept out on.
.launch/
